\section{Discussion and Conclusion}\label{sec:discussion}\label{sec:selection_method}\label{sec:conclusion}

Degeneracy ($12$--$68$\%) limits diversity; signal alignment collapse ($\alpha{\to}0$) limits ranking; $\alpha$ is the binding constraint ($8$--$33{\times}$ tighter; \S\ref{sec:theory}).
Cross-scale validation (4B--72B fine-tuned, GPT/Claude/Gemini zero-shot; Tables~\ref{tab:scale_comparison},~\ref{tab:frontier_sc_cross}) confirms degeneracy is model-family-dependent; failure mechanisms may differ at frontier scale.
In practice, verify $D$ before deploying SC: if $D > 50$\%, greedy decoding is the cost-effective default; entity construction helps only when $D < 20$\% with positive $\alpha$ (Appendix~\ref{app:cost_benefit}).

